      en: "Kent Ridge Park is a 47-hectare park on a 50-meter hill in southwestern Singapore. Named after the Duchess of Kent, it opened in 1956. It is part of the Southern Ridges and features a 1.1 km Canopy Walk through secondary forest. The site has historical importance as a British military base during World War II. The park offers views of the harbour and the west coast, and is popular for bird watching and jogging.",
